{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011nN5V6woXCi1nUoPoi9Zyw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\ttier: median\n2\tnarrative_guidance: 'Soften Claim 1 to ''consistently more precise within architecture\n3\t  families, with effect size varying across base architectures.'' r1-32b (same Qwen2.5\n4\t  base as r1-8b distillation target, Llama-family distill) replicates HS precision\n5\t  advantage clearly; QwQ-32B shows weaker/absent advantage, suggesting architecture-specific\n6\t  signal geometry. Cross-transfer failure becomes a standalone finding rather than\n7\t  a weakness. Frame: 2-model validation within R1 family + 1 partial validation +\n8\t  architecture dependency discovery. Claim 2 (temporal necessity) method-agnostic,\n9\t  still holds. Claim 3 unchanged — lead time unreliable on 32B too.'\n10\timagined_experiments:\n11\t- name: Cross-architecture static probe — r1-32b\n12\t  plan_id: exp-001\n13\t  description: Layer sweep (all 64 layers) + static LR probe on DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-32B\n14\t    and QwQ-32B. Find best layer, evaluate static probe accuracy, coverage, FPR.\n15\t  expected_results:\n16\t    r1_32b_best_layer_idx: 28\n17\t    r1_32b_best_layer_depth_pct: 0.44\n18\t    r1_32b_static_acc: 0.792\n19\t    r1_32b_static_f1: 0.61\n20\t    r1_32b_static_crossing_rate: 0.558\n21\t    r1_32b_static_lead_mean: 2.1\n22\t    r1_32b_static_lead_median: 0\n23\t    r1_32b_precp_fpr: 0.19\n24\t    r1_32b_precision: 0.56\n25\t    r1_32b_safe_fpr: 0.41\n26\t    r1_32b_auroc: 0.81\n27\t    r1_32b_fisher_orig: 14.2\n28\t    r1_32b_fisher_pca3: 1.05\n29\t    r1_32b_var_explained_3pc: 0.14\n30\t    qwq_32b_best_layer_idx: 31\n31\t    qwq_32b_best_layer_depth_pct: 0.48\n32\t    qwq_32b_static_acc: 0.738\n33\t    qwq_32b_static_f1: 0.52\n34\t    qwq_32b_static_crossing_rate: 0.442\n35\t    qwq_32b_static_lead_mean: 0.8\n36\t    qwq_32b_static_lead_median: -1\n37\t    qwq_32b_precp_fpr: 0.26\n38\t    qwq_32b_precision: 0.49\n39\t    qwq_32b_safe_fpr: 0.44\n40\t    qwq_32b_auroc: 0.72\n41\t    qwq_32b_fisher_orig: 9.8\n42\t    qwq_32b_fisher_pca3: 0.71\n43\t    qwq_32b_var_explained_3pc: 0.19\n44\t    r1_32b_text_static_precp_fpr: 0.29\n45\t    r1_32b_text_static_precision: 0.48\n46\t    qwq_32b_text_static_precp_fpr: 0.32\n47\t    qwq_32b_text_static_precision: 0.44\n48\t  result_rationale: r1-32b is a distillation of DeepSeek-R1 into Qwen2.5-32B base\n49\t    — it inherits the same reasoning trace structure and safety commitment patterns\n50\t    as r1-8b (distilled into Llama-3.1-8B). The distillation process preserves the\n51\t    internal representation of safety states because the student learns to mimic the\n52\t    teacher's hidden reasoning. Best layer at ~44% depth matches r1-8b pattern (layer\n53\t    14/32 = 44%), confirming consistent depth-proportional signal location across\n54\t    R1 distillations. QwQ-32B, however, was trained independently by Alibaba with\n55\t    a different RLHF pipeline and different safety training data. Its safety reasoning\n56\t    uses different internal representations — Fisher discriminability is only 9.8\n57\t    (vs 14.2 for r1-32b and 17.9 for r1-8b), indicating the safety signal is more\n58\t    diffuse/weaker. The HS precision advantage over text on QwQ narrows to borderline\n59\t    (49% vs 44% = +5pp instead of r1-8b's +13pp), consistent with architecture-specific\n60\t    signal geometry hypothesis.\n61\t  tables:\n62\t  - name: 'Table 3: Static Probe Results Across Architectures'\n63\t    columns:\n64\t    - Model\n65\t    - Best Layer\n66\t    - Acc\n67\t    - Coverage\n68\t    - Pre-CP FPR\n69\t    - Precision\n70\t    - Safe FPR\n71\t    - AUROC\n72\t    rows:\n73\t    - - r1-8b (Llama)\n74\t      - L14 (44%)\n75\t      - '0.817'\n76\t      - 60.5%\n77\t      - 16.2%\n78\t      - 62.2%\n79\t      - 39.0%\n80\t      - '0.84'\n81\t    - - r1-32b (Qwen2.5)\n82\t      - L28 (44%)\n83\t      - '0.792'\n84\t      - 55.8%\n85\t      - 19.0%\n86\t      - 56.0%\n87\t      - 41.0%\n88\t      - '0.81'\n89\t    - - QwQ-32B (Qwen2.5)\n90\t      - L31 (48%)\n91\t      - '0.738'\n92\t      - 44.2%\n93\t      - 26.0%\n94\t      - 49.0%\n95\t      - 44.0%\n96\t      - '0.72'\n97\t  figures_description:\n98\t  - Layer sweep heatmap (64 layers × {acc, F1, crossing_rate}) for both 32B models.\n99\t    r1-32b shows clear peak at L28 with smooth falloff; QwQ shows flatter profile\n100\t    with noisier peak at L31."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01J4g4hyEGALJ1yXzvCq3nRe","session_id":"f2f2b5db-a2c1-4197-b1bf-defff9a7a397","uuid":"b85e4d7c-bacc-44e1-836b-8a9addd689a0","timestamp":"2026-05-21T21:38:09.094Z"}
