{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FTMGGbdMjTiCkXthMFSQBL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tdream_id: dream_20260512T204322\n2\tproject: structfuse-context\n3\tvenue: ''\n4\tfocus: 'Key risk: dataflow negatives showed connected⊆gold at MVP scale (8 repos)\n5\t  but Z=40.8% at 50-repo scale. Full-scale training may reveal the effect is weaker\n6\t  than hypothesized. Also: embedding-distance negatives actively harm (-3.7pp R@1),\n7\t  which is a strong negative result supporting the dual-pillar motivation. Reviewers\n8\t  should stress-test whether the connected≠gold signal at scale (40.8%) is sufficient\n9\t  to produce meaningful training differentiation, and whether the improvement magnitude\n10\t  will be large enough for EMNLP acceptance.'\n11\treview_mode: full\n12\treview_visible: true\n13\twriting_visible: true\n14\twhat_if: []\n15\ttier_definitions:\n16\t  tiers:\n17\t    best:\n18\t      tier: best\n19\t      meaning: Dataflow negatives produce statistically significant retrieval gains\n20\t        over random; all 3 claims hold; EMNLP Main viable\n21\t      key_assumptions:\n22\t      - Z% at 5K-repo scale ≥ 35%, confirming sufficient connected≠gold signal for\n23\t        meaningful negative mining\n24\t      - Dataflow-aware training converges to different optimum than random (val_loss\n25\t        gap > 0.02)\n26\t      - CodeQL timeout < 8% at 5K scale, extraction remains practical\n27\t      - Embedding-distance harm replicates at full scale (Δ_emb < -2pp R@5)\n28\t      - Gain transfers to end-to-end SWE-bench Lite resolve rate\n29\t      number_ranges:\n30\t        Z_pct_5K:\n31\t        - 35\n32\t        - 50\n33\t        codeql_timeout_pct_5K:\n34\t        - 3\n35\t        - 8\n36\t        retrieval_R5_dataflow:\n37\t        - 0.82\n38\t        - 0.9\n39\t        retrieval_R5_random:\n40\t        - 0.74\n41\t        - 0.82\n42\t        retrieval_R5_emb_dist:\n43\t        - 0.7\n44\t        - 0.78\n45\t    