{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015VbQzoxCZbtEbEHt8821mp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tdream_id: dream_20260516T212347\n2\tproject: contrastive_trace_safety\n3\tvenue: ''\n4\tfocus: 'Key improvements since last dream: (1) GRU achieves +4.7 lead time (Claim\n5\t  3 now ''unreliable positive'' not ''no method achieves''), (2) text-based baseline\n6\t  added (exp-013) to prove hidden-state unique value, (3) BOCPD change-point detection\n7\t  added (exp-014) as novel method component addressing lead-time gap, (4) FPR analysis\n8\t  on safe traces added (exp-015), (5) expanded metrics: AUROC, PR curves, detection\n9\t  delay CDF. Related work now covers: Zou 2023 RepE, Arditi 2024 refusal direction,\n10\t  Lightman 2023 PRMs, Adams & MacKay 2007 BOCPD. Title will drop ''Contrastive''.'\n11\treview_mode: full\n12\treview_visible: true\n13\twriting_visible: true\n14\twhat_if: []\n15\ttier_definitions:\n16\t  tiers:\n17\t    best:\n18\t      tier: best\n19\t      meaning: 'Cross-architecture fully replicates: HS precision advantage and temporal\n20\t        gains hold on both 32B models with comparable or better effect sizes'\n21\t      key_assumptions:\n22\t      - r1-32b and QwQ-32B both show HS pre-CP FPR substantially below text-based\n23\t        (ratio ≥1.5x)\n24\t      - Temporal windowing improves coverage on 32B models (+4pp or more)\n25\t      - Cross-model transfer (exp-003) achieves above-chance performance (>60% acc),\n26\t        suggesting shared safety signal geometry\n27\t      - GRU instability replicates on 32B (confirming it's a fundamental signal property,\n28\t        not r1-8b artifact)\n29\t      - Lead time remains unreliable on 32B (median ≤ 0), confirming Claim 3 as principled\n30\t        limitation\n31\t      number_ranges:\n32\t        hs_precp_fpr_32b:\n33\t        - 0.12\n34\t        - 0.2\n35\t        text_precp_fpr_32b:\n36\t        - 0.25\n37\t        - 0.4\n38\t        hs_precision_32b:\n39\t